The legal texts come from EswatiniLII (the Judiciary of Eswatini, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  EswatiniLII, https://eswatinilii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as EswatiniLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting EswatiniLII as the source (https://eswatinilii.org/terms-of-use/).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: EswatiniLII (https://eswatinilii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws EswatiniLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither EswatiniLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Texts added from November 2026 come from further sources, each under its own terms:

  Judiciary of Eswatini, https://www.judiciary.org.sz/legislation: official texts of Acts and court rules,
  published by the Judiciary for public use.

  Government of Eswatini, https://www.gov.sz and https://parliament.gov.sz: official Acts, Gazettes and legal
  notices, read from Internet Archive copies (https://web.archive.org) because the hosts no longer answer.
  Official legislative texts are public law.

  FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, https://faolex.fao.org: reuse for
  non-commercial purposes with acknowledgement of FAO as the source (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/).
  Source: FAOLEX Database, FAO.

  WIPO Lex, World Intellectual Property Organization, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex: national laws as
  collected by WIPO; the texts are the member State's official legislation (https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html).

Commits from these sources name the source in their Source: trailer, and secondary copies carry a
Source-status: trailer.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
